  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resettlement Programme with the Government of Romania from Jordan, Lebanon and Turkey in 2021-2022 (STARRT IV) - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is to contribute to the provision of a durable solution to 200 beneficiaries of international protection in Jordan, Lebanon and Turkey by facilitating their resettlement to Romania. IOM has the specific expertise and capacity required to successfully deliver the project based on extensive experience in movement management and resettlement processing. IOM aims to achieve the project&apos;s objective by providing support to selection missions, conducting pre-migration health activities and delivering pre-departure orientation sessions, as well as ensuring the safe and dignified movement of the project beneficiaries to Romania.</narrative>
  </description>
